gpu_skip_unchanged_constant_writes (on by default): when the game rewrites float, bool, loop or fetch constants with the
values they already have, the D3D12 command processor keeps the uploaded constant buffers, the texture bindings and the
sampler memo instead of rebuilding them for the next draw. Vertex buffer residency is still reset on every fetch
constant write, since the game may have rewritten the vertex data at the same address.

